    "answer": {
      "short": "The digit sum stays $A+B+C+D$, so every four-digit rearrangement is divisible by 3. Excluding $\\overline{ABCD}$ and $\\overline{BDAC}$, the candidate arrangements are: ABDC, ACBD, ACDB, ADBC, ADCB; BACD, BADC, BCAD, BCDA, BDCA; CABD, CADB, CBAD, CBDA, CDAB, CDBA; DABC, DACB, DBAC, DBCA, DCAB, DCBA. Omit arrangements beginning with zero, repeated numerical values, and either original number.",
